// Original work, written for STORYMACHINE_STRUCTURAL_FORM_EXPERIMENT_2026-08-03.
// Three-act CONTROL, Pair 2 (n=16 scenes), matched to
// pair2-kishotenketsu.fountain: same protagonist, setting, scene count, and
// prose register — restructured around structure-presets.ts's three_act
// template (Act One 0-22%, Inciting 22-28%, Act Two 28-72%, Climax 72-86%,
// Act Three 86-100%). Scenes 1-3 are textually identical to the
// kishotenketsu arm; the antagonist and escalating conflict enter at scene 4,
// exactly where the beat maps diverge, and the story resolves with a public
// confrontation and a clear winner and loser, unlike the kishotenketsu arm's
// synthesis ending.

INT. AMARO CONSERVATION STUDIO - MORNING

Tall north-facing windows, even gray light. YUKI AMARO, mid-30s, leans over a slanted table with a bone folder and a jeweler's loupe, easing a brittle fold flat on a hundred-year-old atlas page. Wheat paste, brushes, weighted sandbags arranged with surgical precision.

YUKI
(not looking up)
Come around from the left. The light's better and you won't cast a shadow on the seam.

She works the fold another millimeter, exhales.

INT. STUDIO - STORAGE ROOM - CONTINUOUS

Shelves of flat archival boxes, each labeled in careful block print. Yuki slides one free: THORN COLLECTION — 1947 REPRINT, VOL. 3. She holds it a moment before carrying it out, the way you'd hold something that used to belong to someone.

INT. STUDIO - MAIN ROOM - LATER

DEV OKAFOR, 20s, apprentice, sets two coffees down without being asked and peers at the open atlas.

DEV
Thorn's the one you trained under?

YUKI
Nineteen years. He restored this exact volume in '91, before I ever touched a bone folder. I'm just re-lining page thirty-four. Foxing's spread since the last treatment.

DEV
Feels like restoring someone's restoration.

YUKI
It usually is, eventually. That's the job.

INT. STUDIO - MAIN ROOM - AFTERNOON

MARGO OYELARAN, 50s, auction house liaison, arrives unannounced with a folder of photographs, sets them down hard enough to rattle the loupe.

MARGO
Someone's consigning a second "original" 1947 Thorn atlas at Kessler's. Near-identical to yours. Your provenance signature's on both files.

YUKI
There's only one original. It's on this table.

MARGO
Then someone's using your name to sell the other one.

INT. STUDIO - MAIN ROOM - EVENING

Yuki and Dev dig through client records and backup drives. One external drive — restoration notes, technique photographs, four months of documentation — is missing from its labeled slot. No break-in reported; nothing "valuable" seemed to be taken at the time.

DEV
Nobody flagged this because nobody thought notes were worth stealing.

YUKI
Somebody did.

INT. AUCTION HOUSE - PREVIEW ROOM - DAY

Yuki examines the rival atlas under glass, gloved. The repair technique is uncannily hers — same wheat-paste ratio, same stitch along the spine. Margo watches from across the room, arms crossed, no longer entirely on Yuki's side.

MARGO
Convince me this isn't yours.

YUKI
It's my technique. It is not my work.

EXT. CITY STREET - DAY

Across four lanes of traffic, Yuki spots CALLUM REYES, late 20s, a folder under his arm, climbing into a cab before she can cross. Their eyes meet for one second through the window as it pulls away.

YUKI
(to Dev, breathless)
That's Callum.

INT. STUDIO - MAIN ROOM - NIGHT

Yuki lays it out for Dev, pacing.

YUKI
Callum apprenticed here two years. I let him go for cutting corners on lining work. He had drive access the month the drive went missing.

DEV
So he's not just copying your technique. He's selling it as your name.

INT. AUCTION HOUSE - MARGO'S OFFICE - DAY

Margo, cornered by pressure from the consignor, lays it out flat.

MARGO
Friday's sale, lot forty-one. Bring me hard forensic proof it's a forgery before the gavel, or I pull every one of your consignments and every referral I've ever sent you.

YUKI
And if I can't get proof by Friday?

MARGO
Then as far as this house is concerned, the fraud's yours to answer for, not his.

INT. STUDIO - MAIN ROOM - NIGHT

Yuki and Dev run ink-aging tests on a paper sample smuggled from the preview room, comparing spectra on a laptop screen. The ink is modern, deliberately mixed to mimic period oxidation — close enough to fool a casual eye, not close enough to fool a spectrometer.

DEV
It's good. It's just not old.

YUKI
Good enough to sell. Not good enough to survive a UV pass.

INT. STUDIO - MAIN ROOM - NIGHT (LATER)

Yuki's phone buzzes: an unknown number, a photo attachment of her own stolen notebook pages, captioned CAREFUL WHOSE NAME YOU PUT ON THINGS. Dev reads it over her shoulder. Outside, Friday is two days away.

DEV
He knows you're close.

YUKI
Then we get closer.

INT. AUCTION HOUSE - SALE FLOOR - DAY (FRIDAY)

Bidding underway on lot forty-one. Callum sits near the front, composed, a paddle balanced on his knee. Yuki strides down the aisle with Dev and a folder of forensic results, interrupting the auctioneer mid-call.

YUKI
Lot forty-one is a forgery. I can prove it to everyone in this room, right now.

A ripple through the crowd. Callum doesn't move, but his knuckles whiten on the paddle.

INT. AUCTION HOUSE - SALE FLOOR - CONTINUOUS

Yuki lays the ink-aging results across the podium and pulls up a UV scan on a tablet: a fingerprint smudge embedded beneath a "period" repair — Callum's own print, left copying her stitch pattern too carefully. Callum tries to argue provenance; his voice thins under the room's stare. Security moves in. He's escorted out past rows of turned heads.

CALLUM
(low, passing her)
You always did check your seams too closely.

YUKI
Somebody had to teach me that.

INT. STUDIO - MAIN ROOM - DAY (LATER)

Yuki's phone on speaker; Margo's voice, brisk and relieved.

MARGO (V.O.)
Consignments are reinstated. The forged atlas is pulled from record, permanently.

Yuki sets the phone down and finally sits.

INT. STUDIO - MAIN ROOM - DAY

Yuki and Dev return the real atlas to its archival box. A locksmith finishes installing a new deadbolt on the storage room door, hands Yuki two keys.

DEV
Only two copies this time.

YUKI
Only two people who need one.

INT. STUDIO - MAIN ROOM - DUSK

Yuki labels a fresh box in careful block print: AMARO CONSERVATION — VERIFIED, and sets it on the shelf beside the others. She switches off the lamp, the studio quiet, the threat gone.
